A command whose ignore file holds entries of two other languages' schemes, one
of them outside that language's reference grammar and one naming a quoted
member that holds a space, each in the shape every document checks. Neither
scheme is this analyzer's to read, so the run accepts every entry unread and
counts none.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- deadset-ignore.json --
{"ignore": [
  {"code": "DS1002", "symbol": "ts://app/src/index.ts#not..a..reference", "path": "src/index.ts", "reason": "the TypeScript analyzer's"},
  {"code": "DS1003", "symbol": "ts://app/src/index.ts#Headers.'content type'", "path": "src/index.ts", "reason": "the TypeScript analyzer's"},
  {"code": "DS1002", "symbol": "proto://pkg#Thing", "path": "thing.proto", "reason": "the schema reader's"}
]}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}
